-- 1000641 RM-PAPER-PROVENANCE-TRACE-1
UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'FIRST STEP (ROADMAP-DOERS-EB-1, 2026-10-28): in publishStageV2, after the paper row is prepared and before the paper is made public, build one JSON provenance record {seed, trace_id, novelty} and store it with the paper change (read docs/PAPER-LEDGER.md for paper_change_bodies and change_actor/change_reason first). seed is the research_queue row id and its generation parameters, trace_id the id of the logged events of the run (logEvent ids of the stages), novelty the result of the novelty check the pipeline already runs (null with the reason when none ran). Never put prompt text or secrets in the record. Offline test with a stub env. Mark with a comment containing PAPER-PROVENANCE-TRACE-1. A later task adds the view that counts the share of new papers carrying the record and the link on the paper page; this issue closes on that share, not on this step.' || char(10) || 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-research-exec/worker.js' || char(10) || 'code-anchor: async function publishStageV2(env, row) {' WHERE id = 1000641 AND status = 'open' AND description NOT LIKE '%code-task:%';

-- 1000648 RM-CITE-EXISTENCE-GATE-1
UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'FIRST STEP (ROADMAP-DOERS-EB-1, 2026-10-28): the gate already exists for arXiv ids, DOIs and URLs (CITATION_GATE in qnfo-research-exec: lookupArxiv, lookupDoi with the Crossref title, lookupUrl). Crossref use is in this gate (api.crossref.org/works), so reuse it. The gap is a reference with none of those: add resolveByTitleYear(ref, fetchFn) that queries Crossref works with query.bibliographic=<title> and a from-pub-date/until-pub-date window of the stated year plus or minus one, accepts the top hit when titleAgrees passes, and otherwise returns state not-found (no hit) or error (HTTP failure). A flagged reference is held through the existing unverified/retry path and never dropped. Export it in the returned object and call it from citationGate for refs of kind other. Offline tests with a stub fetch: a real reference resolves, an invented one is flagged, a Crossref 500 gives unverified not failure. Mark with a comment containing RM-CITE-EXISTENCE-GATE-1. Precision and recall against the published-reference fixture are a later task and are what closes this issue.' || char(10) || 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-research-exec/worker.js' || char(10) || 'code-anchor: return { citationGate: citationGate, describeFailures: describeFailures, extractRefs: extractRefs, titleAgrees: titleAgrees };' WHERE id = 1000648 AND status = 'open' AND description NOT LIKE '%code-task:%';

-- 1000649 RM-POLICY-SMT-GATE-1
UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'FIRST STEP (ROADMAP-DOERS-EB-1, 2026-10-28): shadow mode first, as the issue requires. In qnfo-ops execTool, before dispatch, call policyGateShadow(env, name, args) that evaluates hand-written predicates (plain JavaScript, no model, no solver yet; a Worker cannot load Z3) for three irreversible tool classes: email send, publish, delete. Each rule has an id, a pure function of the tool name and args, and a reason. In shadow mode (ops_config policy_gate_mode, default shadow) it never blocks: it writes one cloud_ops_events row kind policy-gate-shadow with the tool, rule id and would_block, wrapped so a failure of the gate cannot fail the tool call. Enforcement is a later task that needs the measured precision and recall on replayed ops_ai_log calls. Offline test: each rule blocks its bad case and passes its good case. Mark with a comment containing POLICY-GATE-1:shadow. Extends BP26-PROMPT-INJECTION-1 (1000359) and the MODEL-ONLY rows of docs/DETERMINISTIC-GATE-AUDIT.md. Closes on the replay measurement.' || char(10) || 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-ops/worker.js' || char(10) || 'code-anchor: async function execTool(env, name, rawArgs, userText, resultCap) {' WHERE id = 1000649 AND status = 'open' AND description NOT LIKE '%code-task:%';

